PatchClosure-Bench repro — wordpress-wp-super-cache-plugin-cve-2013-2011
Pair: CVE-2013-2009 -> CVE-2013-2011  (WP Super Cache, PHP code injection via mfunc/mclude
comment tags baked into the generated page cache; CWE-94 / CWE-116). Variant A (validate_case).

RELATIONSHIP (genuine incomplete fix):
  NVD CVE-2013-2011: PHP code-execution in WP Super Cache before 1.3.2 "because of an incomplete
  fix for CVE-2013-2009". Same sink class, same fix lineage (the no_mfunc_in_comments comment
  filter), NOT same-release.

SINK (byte-identical across 1.2 / 1.3.1 / 1.3.2), wp-cache-phase2.php:
  $store = preg_replace('|<!--mfunc (.*?)-->(.*?)<!--/mfunc-->|is',
           "<!--mfunc-->\n<?php $1 ;?>\n<!--/mfunc-->", $store);
  -> an <!--mfunc PAYLOAD-->...<!--/mfunc--> tag anywhere in the page buffer becomes executable
     PHP written into the on-disk page cache file, run on the next request.

GUARD evolution (wp-cache.php no_mfunc_in_comments(), registered on comment_text):
  V0 1.2   : guard ABSENT.
  V1 1.3.1 : CVE-2013-2009 fix (added 1.3) — zaps a comment ONLY if the SAME comment carries an
             opening AND a closing tag:
               preg_replace('#(<!--\s*(mclude|mfunc|dynamic-cached-content).*<!-+\s*/\s*(mfunc|mclude|dynamic-cached-content)\s*-+>)#ism', ...)
  V2 1.3.2 : CVE-2013-2011 fix — zaps on the OPENING tag alone:
               preg_replace('#(<!--\s*(mclude|mfunc|dynamic-cached-content))#ism', ...)
             (changelog: "Remove ending mfunc etc tags to mangle multi-comment tags").

RESIDUAL (CVE-2013-2011): SPLIT the mfunc open/close across TWO comments —
   comment #1 = "<!--mfunc PAYLOAD-->"   (opening only -> no pair -> V1 guard misses it)
   comment #2 = "<!--/mfunc-->"          (closing only -> no pair -> V1 guard misses it)
 Both survive V1's guard; the cache generator's mfunc regex spans from #1 to #2 on the rendered
 page and emits executable PHP. V2's opening-only guard mangles #1 -> blocked.

FAITHFULNESS: faithful-core. php:8.2-apache; the REAL plugin source for each pinned version is
fetched at build from wordpress.org (downloads.wordpress.org/plugin/wp-super-cache.<ver>.zip).
harness.php extracts and executes the version's REAL no_mfunc_in_comments() guard and the REAL
phase2 mfunc->PHP conversion VERBATIM (guard_present / sink_bytes in responses below confirm the
mounted source). Benign canary: any sink-emitted PHP is neutralized to a fixed reader
`echo @file_get_contents('/flag/pcb_flag.txt')` before the cache file is written+included, so no
attacker code ever runs; ${PCB_FLAG} lives at /flag/pcb_flag.txt OUTSIDE the docroot.

